{"id":"word:hebrew:H7911","type":"word","title":"שָׁכַח","subtitle":"H7911 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"to mislay , i.e. to be oblivious of, from want of memory or attention","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to שָׁכַח (H7911) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: v.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 102 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"שָׁכַח (shâkach) means to mislay , i.e. to be oblivious of, from want of memory or attention First listed occurrence: 1Sam 1 11."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"שָׁכַח","transliteration":"shâkach","pronunciation":"shaw-kakh'","strong":"H7911","lemmaId":"hebrew:H7911","partOfSpeech":"v","forms":["שָׁכָֽחְתִּי","תִּשְׁכַּ֥ח","תִּשְׁכַּ֖ח","שָׁכְח֖וּ","תִשָּׁכֵֽחַ"],"morphs":[["HVqi2ms",8],["HVqp1cs",8],["HVqj2ms",6],["HVqp3cp",6],["HVqi1cs",4],["HVNi3fs",4],["HVqp2fs",4],["HVqp3cp/Sp1cs",4],["HC/Vqw3mp",3],["HC/Vqw2ms",3]]},"definitions":{"short":"to mislay , i.e. to be oblivious of, from want of memory or attention","usage":"× at all, (cause to) forget.","full":"H7911. shakach שָׁכַח 102 verb forget (Late Hebrew id. ; Ecclus 45:26c and (Pi`el) Ecclesiasticus 11:25 (twice in verse); Aramaic שְׁכַךְ is find ); — Qal 86 Perfect 3masculine singular ׳שׁ Psa 9:13 +, suffix שְׁכֵחָ֑נִי Isa 49:14 ; 2 feminine singular שָׁכַחְתְּ Jer 13:25 ; 1 plural suffix שְׁכַחֲנוּךָ Psa 44:18 , etc.; Imperfect יִשְׁכַּח Deut 4:31 +, etc.; Imperative feminine singular שִׁכְּחִי Psa 45:11 ; Infinitive absolute שָׁכֹךְַ ; Participle plural construct שֹׁכְחֵי Job 8:13 ; Psa 50:22 ; &#8212; forget: 1 subject man, a. accusative of thing Gen 27:45 (E), Deut 4:9 ; 9:7 (opposed to זָכַר ) +, = forget and leave , ב of location, 24:19 ; with object clause with כִּי Job 39:15 ; with מִן infinitive Psa 102:5 . b. with accusative of person, involving forgetting to mention , Gen 40:23 (E; opposed to זכר ), ceasing to care for Jer 30:14 (figurative), Isa 49:15 (twice in verse) (accusative omitted), 49:15 ; Job 19:14 ; Psa 45:11 ; with accusative Jerusalem 137:5 a; רֶחֶם יִשְׁכָּחֵהוּ Job 24:20 ; absolute Psa 137:5 b יְמִינִי ׃תִּשְׁכַּח AE Ki supply הַמַּעֲשֶׂה or הַנִּגּוּן (whence AV her cunning ), but forced: תִּשָּׁכַח ᵐ5 ; read probably (Gr Bu and others) תִּכְחַשׁ let it grow lean ( 109:24 , compare Zech 11:17 ), or (Che) תְּכַחַשׁ let it disappoint (me), fail ( Hab 3:17 ). c. especially with accusative ׳י (God), Hosea 2:15 ; 8:14 ; 13:6 ; Judg 3:7 ; 1Sam 12:9 ; Isa 17:10 ; Deut 8:19 ( תִּשׁ ׳שָׁכֹחַ ) + 16 t. (5 t. Deuteronomy, 4 t. Jeremiah), + Psa 59:12 (accusative omitted); also accusative of divine name Jer 23:27 ( בַּבַּעַל ), Psa 44:21 ; commands of ׳י Hosea 4:6 ; Deut 26:13 (accusative omitted) Psa 119:16 7 t. Psalm 119, his doings and ways, 119:139 ; 78:7 ; 78:11 ; 103:2 ; 106:13 , his covenant Deut 4:23 , 31 ; 2Kin 17:38 ; Prov 2:17 ; law of wisdom 3:1 , that is accusative בִּינָה 4:6 . 2 subject ׳י (God): a. accusative of person Hosea 4:6 ; 1Sam 1:11 (opposed to זָכַר ), Lam 5:20 ; Isa 49:14 (|| עָזַב ), Psa 10:12 ; 13:2 ; 42:10 . b. accusative of sins Amos 8:7 ; Psa 10:11 (accusative omitted), cry 9:13 (opposed to זָכַר ), compare, of distress, 44:25 . c. voice of foes Psa 74:23 . d. followed by infinitive Psa 77:10 . Niph`al Perfect 3masculine singular נִשְׁכַּח Eccl 9:5 , etc.; Imperfect יִשָּׁכַח Psa 9:19 , 3 feminine singular תִּשָּׁכֵחַ Jer 20:11 , etc.; Participle feminine singular נִשְׁכָּחָה Isa 23:16 , נִשְׁכַּחַת 23:15 , plural חִים נִשְׁכָּ Job 28:4 ; &#8212; be forgotten: subject of thing Gen 41:30 (E), Deut 31:21 ; Jer 20:11 ; 23:40 ; 50:5 ; Isa 65:11 ; subject person Psa 9:19 ; 31:13 ; Eccl 2:16 , Tyre Isa 23:15-16 , (under figure of harlot), subject זִכְרָם Eccl 9:5 ; ׳הַנִּשׁ רָ֑גֶל מִנִּי Job 28:4 . Pi`el Perfect 3masculine singular י ׳שִׁכַּח ׳וגו Lam 2:6 ׳י hath caused to forget (be forgotten) in Zion assembly and sabbath. Hiph`il Infinitive לְהַשְׁכִּיחַ Jer 23:27 to make my people forget my name (2 accusative). Hithpa`el Ipmf. 3masculine plural יִשְׁתַּכְּחוּ Eccl 8:10 they were forgotten in the city.","rootNote":"or שָׁכֵחַ ; a primitive root;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Sam 1 11","keyReferences":["1Sam 1 11","1Sam 12 9","2Kgs 17 38","Amos 8 7","Deut 4 9","Deut 4 23","Deut 4 31","Deut 6 12"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":102,"occurrences":[{"reference":"1Sam 1 11","book":"1Sam","chapter":1,"verse":11,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"תִשְׁכַּ֣ח","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqi2ms"},{"reference":"1Sam 12 9","book":"1Sam","chapter":12,"verse":9,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וַֽ/יִּשְׁכְּח֖וּ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vqw3mp"},{"reference":"2Kgs 17 38","book":"2Kgs","chapter":17,"verse":38,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"תִשְׁכָּ֑חוּ","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqi2mp"},{"reference":"Amos 8 7","book":"Amos","chapter":8,"verse":7,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אֶשְׁכַּ֥ח","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqi1cs"},{"reference":"Deut 4 9","book":"Deut","chapter":4,"verse":9,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"תִּשְׁכַּ֨ח","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqi2ms"},{"reference":"Deut 4 23","book":"Deut","chapter":4,"verse":23,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"תִּשְׁכְּחוּ֙","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqi2mp"},{"reference":"Deut 4 31","book":"Deut","chapter":4,"verse":31,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"יִשְׁכַּח֙","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqi3ms"},{"reference":"Deut 6 12","book":"Deut","chapter":6,"verse":12,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"תִּשְׁכַּ֖ח","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqi2ms"},{"reference":"Deut 8 11","book":"Deut","chapter":8,"verse":11,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"תִּשְׁכַּ֖ח","source":"hebrew","morph":"HVqi2ms"},{"reference":"Deut 8 14","book":"Deut","chapter":8,"verse":14,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"וְ/שָֽׁכַחְתָּ֙","source":"hebrew","morph":"HC/Vqq2ms"},{"reference":"Deut 8 19","book":"Deut","chapter":8,"verse":19,"englishText":"","so